WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.330
Speaker 1: All right, as many of you know,
I am fascinated by scams, and it just so happens

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.110
that the former president and the current
Republican Party have perpetrated a number

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.530
of different scams, not only on the American
people generally, but on their own followers

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.530
and donors.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.909
We've talked about fundraising scams before.

00:00:18.909 --> 00:00:24.169
One such scam was that after the 2020 election,
Donald Trump claimed to be raising money

00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:27.589
Speaker 2: for fighting
Speaker 1: the election results for overturning

00:00:27.589 --> 00:00:28.589
the election.

00:00:28.589 --> 00:00:34.010
Speaker 2: And you could donate, presumably
Speaker 1: to audits and recounts and whatever

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.010
else.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.220
Now that was a scam on its
Speaker 2: face, obviously, because they weren't

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.690
going to
Speaker 1: overturn the election, but there

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.670
were other layers on which it was a scam as
well.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:49.530
For example, in the fine print, when Trump
was raising money to overturn the election

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.030
results, depending on the promo, you would
look at the fine print and it would say 50

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.470
percent of your donation.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:01:00.130
60 percent of your donation can be used
Speaker 2: not to fighting

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:04.370
Speaker 1: to overturn the election, but to
pay off Trump's campaign

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:07.159
Speaker 2: debt
Speaker 1: prior to the election.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:10.329
The scam
Speaker 2: was some pre-check

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:15.369
Speaker 1: boxes when you would make what
you thought was a one time donation to Trump.

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:20.259
One of the boxes that was automatically checked
unless you uncheck it, is that you're committing

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:23.509
to an ongoing donation, even
Speaker 2: though you meant to make a single.

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:27.659
Speaker 1: And the second box was that in
some cases the amount would go up.

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:32.329
Whatever your donation, there would be like
a multiplier of some kind added on in the

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:33.439
subsequent donation.

00:01:33.439 --> 00:01:36.609
So that was another scam that they did.

00:01:36.609 --> 00:01:40.869
There's a new scam now, or at least it has
returned.

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:45.229
The new scam is that the NRC that's the
Speaker 2: National Republican

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:49.070
Speaker 1: Republican Senatorial Committee
Speaker 2: is running a

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.439
Speaker 1: promo called
Speaker 2: Dinner with Trump.

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:56.459
Speaker 1: Now, if I say to you, we are running
a have dinner with me

00:01:56.459 --> 00:01:59.319
Speaker 2: promo, would you
Speaker 1: expect me to be at the dinner?

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.099
I think so.

00:02:01.099 --> 00:02:03.341
If I ran a promo
Speaker 2: called Have dinner

00:02:03.341 --> 00:02:05.060
Speaker 1: with my mom.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.320
Would you expect my mom
Speaker 2: to be at the dinner?

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.440
Yes, I think so.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:15.690
Speaker 1: If a celebrity chef like our friend
Tyler Florence runs a Have Dinner with Tyler

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.620
promo, would you expect him to be there?

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.850
Speaker 2: I would.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:23.260
Speaker 1: But the dinner with Trump?

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.930
Dinner doesn't have Trump.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.580
This is a huge thing.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.040
They're promoting it as enter to win dinner
with Trump.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.420
Do you want to have dinner with President
Trump?

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.660
Enter now for your chance to meet President
Trump.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:44.430
But then you pull out the fine print and it
says a winner and a guest will have a private

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:51.260
dinner with senators Lindsey Graham Tim Scott.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.760
And Rick Scott, that there's no mention of
Trump.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:03:03.910
Trump won't be at the dinner for the winner
of the dinner with Trump promo or giveaway.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:09.850
Judd Legum or Legum has been researching this,
and apparently this is a common scam that

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:13.670
Trump and Republicans ran during the 2020
campaign.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.380
There were all these promos lunch with Trump
in Chicago.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.240
Dinner with Trump in Cleveland.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.850
All of this stuff now.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:28.150
Is it possible some of these events happened
and Trump had lunch or dinner with somebody

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.150
that won the thing?

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.850
You know, he had lunch or dinner, but with
some of the people who actually entered?

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:32.850
Maybe.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.530
But there is no evidence that we're able to
find that any of these events actually took

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.530
place.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.350
Now I want to be really clear,
Speaker 2: I don't care about the

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:44.760
Speaker 1: people getting scammed here in
the sense that if you're willing, willing

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:49.620
to do anything to help Trump and these Republicans
win, donate

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.350
Speaker 2: whatever for a meal with
Speaker 1: Trump.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:58.319
Arguably you've been scammed merely by the
fact that you're supporting this corrupt party.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:01.870
Speaker 2: So like missing the dinner,
Speaker 1: it's kind of the cherry on top

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.100
of the scam.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.010
But shouldn't there be repercussions here?

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:09.010
Because if you run a lottery and nobody wins,
you just collect the money that's illegal.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:14.760
When you do giveaways, raffles, et cetera,
these things are governed by a bunch of different

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:20.889
law, and it's taken pretty seriously in most
cases when you are Trump, I guess, or the

00:04:20.889 --> 00:04:24.230
National Republican Senate Committee or whatever
it is that

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.050
Speaker 2: they're called, everything is a
scam.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:32.030
Speaker 1: The campaign itself, the promises
that were made but not kept the presidency

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.120
itself, the fundraising.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.730
Now even the giveaways are a scam as well.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.230
They should be held accountable.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:05:03.970
No evidence that they 

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:26.639
are 
going 

00:05:26.639 --> 00:05:49.410
to be.

